.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH speedqx 1  "speedqx 3.0.9"
.SH NAME
speedqx \- SpeedQX Internet Speed Test \- QubeTX Developer Tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBspeedqx\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-fastcom\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-latency\-probes\fR] [\fB\-\-update\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SpeedQX Internet Speed Test \- QubeTX Developer Tools
.PP
Quad\-provider speed test using Cloudflare, M\-Lab NDT7, LibreSpeed, and fast.com (Netflix).
All four providers run and results are aggregated for maximum accuracy.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output results as JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR
Use ASCII characters instead of Unicode box\-drawing
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colored output
.SH "SPEED TEST"
.TP
\fB\-\-duration\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 30]
Test duration per direction for CF/NDT7/LibreSpeed: seconds or "auto"
.TP
\fB\-\-fastcom\-duration\fR \fI<FASTCOM_DURATION>\fR [default: auto]
Test duration per direction for fast.com: seconds or "auto" (default: auto)
.TP
\fB\-\-latency\-probes\fR \fI<LATENCY_PROBES>\fR [default: 20]
Number of latency probes
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-update\fR
Check for updates and install the latest version (legacy flag form of `speedqx update`)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
speedqx\-update(1)
Check for updates and install the latest release
.TP
speedqx\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  speedqx                     Run full speed test (all 4 providers)
  speedqx \-\-duration 60       60s per direction for CF/NDT7/LS
  speedqx \-\-fastcom\-duration 30  Override fast.com to 30s/dir
  speedqx update              Check for updates and install
  speedqx \-\-update            Same as \*(Aqspeedqx update\*(Aq (legacy flag form)
  speedqx \-\-json              Output results as JSON

Run \*(Aqspeedqx \-\-help\*(Aq for full details, or \*(Aqspeedqx \-h\*(Aq for a summary.
